# Copy to kit/.env and fill in, or let kit/setup.sh write it. The kit's scripts read it; git and Docker builds never
# see it.
#
# By default the kit needs nothing here, and runs no model: everything runs in containers on this machine, a small
# GitHub, GitLab and Jenkins among them, with no account and no key, and every script it runs is kept.
#   ask   kit/setup.sh asks (the default); for a key this file holds, it asks whether to use it
#   yes   kit/setup.sh uses it, and only says so; kit/setup.sh writes yes for what you opt in to
#   no    kit/setup.sh leaves it off, and only says so
# GitLab is on unless you opt out: it wants about 4 GB more of Docker's memory (about 10 GB in all).
USE_GITLAB=ask
# Your GitHub account and an Anthropic key are opt in. With USE_GITHUB=yes, kit/try.sh works on OWNER/REPO on real
# GitHub; otherwise on acme/web at the small GitHub in the kit.
USE_GITHUB=ask
USE_ANTHROPIC=ask

# Your GitHub account: the repository the kit works on, an empty one of your own, and a fine-grained token for that
# repository alone (github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new): Repository access "Only select repositories",
# the one below; permissions Issues, Pull requests and Contents, read and write.
OWNER=your-github-user
REPO=kit-trial
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# An Anthropic key (console.anthropic.com), for the goals Claude walks on your repository. Replays of kept scripts
# don't need it, but triage's one reasoned step does.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
